/*  firstUseT -- runRule GATES ON hasNewParse AND NEVER INSTALLS A PARSE.

    ⚠⚠ RE-PINNED 2026-09-18, AND THE RE-PIN IS A WITHDRAWAL, NOT A REGRESSION. Tony
    withdrew the first-use install ruled on 2026-09-17: runRule was compiling and installing
    a rule's parse on first use, and that is generation happening inside the gate. Generation
    is EXPLICIT, through `parser`. runRule only asks whether it already happened.
    docs/fixIts.md F-83 ruling 2 carries the withdrawal; the doctrine under it is that calls
    go DOWN and never up -- kant calls C++ verbs, C++ fires installed slots, and C++ never
    resolves an incant action by name.

    ⚠ WHAT THIS FIXTURE ASSERTS NOW IS THE CELL THE WITHDRAWN INSTALL USED TO ACT ON, read
    with values rather than by absence (rule H4): after driving a rule that has a code body
    and no generated parse, `list` reads isCodeD 1 and hasNewParsE 0. Those were exactly the
    two flags the install forked on. It fires nothing, so nothing changes them.

    THE ROWS
      FU-1  testList's own line -- the driver ran. The anti-vacuity sibling for everything
            below: without it a quiet run would satisfy the rest by accident.
      FU-2  isCodeD = 1. THE NON-ZERO SIBLING, and it is not decoration -- FU-2b wants a
            zero, and a zero-expecting row that a dead read would also produce asserts
            nothing. This one fails unless the flag read reaches a real node.
      FU-2b hasNewParsE = 0. THE CLAIM: driving the rule did NOT install a parse.
      FU-2c the miss control -- the same read against a name that does not exist reads 0,
            so FU-2b's zero cannot be a lookup that silently found nothing.

    ⚠ FU-3 RETIRED WITH ITS SUBJECT, 2026-09-18, NOT REGRESSED. It pinned F-83's label gap
    -- `nextGroup: ERROR DatA does not contain a list` -- which is reachable only AFTER the
    rule's body fires, and with the install withdrawn the body does not fire. The row's
    subject is gone, so the row goes rather than being pinned at an absence. F-83's second
    half is unchanged in docs/fixIts.md and the row comes back the day explicit generation
    reaches `list`.

    ⚠ AND ONE MEASUREMENT BANKED HERE BECAUSE IT WAS FOUND HERE: `list` LIVES IN UnitTests,
    NOT IN Grokking. `Grokking["list"]` reads 0 and `UnitTests["list"]` reads 1, with a
    never-defined name reading 0 as the control. That is Tony's own suspicion from the
    2026-09-17 seal, measured -- and it is why the reads below name UnitTests.  */
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search UnitTests Utilities list;
register(UnitTests);
define
    fuFlag;
    fuReport code={
        fuFlag = 0;
        if UnitTests["list"].isCodeD;           fuFlag = 1;
        cerr "FU-2  list isCodeD        = " fuFlag:;
        fuFlag = 0;
        if UnitTests["list"].hasNewParsE;       fuFlag = 1;
        cerr "FU-2b list hasNewParsE    = " fuFlag:;
        fuFlag = 0;
        if UnitTests["zzzNotARule"].isCodeD;    fuFlag = 1;
        cerr "FU-2c miss control isCodeD= " fuFlag:;
        };
    ;
testList();
fuReport();
cerr "FIRSTUSE SENTINEL":;
stop();
